# Line endings are a property of this project, not of each contributor's Git
# installation.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF
# on every platform. Without this the behaviour depends on the machine: the
# Git for Windows installer sets core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which
# rewrites the working tree to CRLF on checkout and normalises back on commit.
# Two things follow from that, and both have bitten this repository:
#
#   - with core.safecrlf=true, which the same installer sets, "git add" fails
#     outright on any file an editor or tool happened to write with LF, because
#     the LF -> index -> CRLF round trip is not reversible;
#
#   - a file whose blob was committed with CRLF from a machine where the
#     conversion was off is silently renormalised the next time anyone touches
#     it, turning a one-line change into a whole-file diff.
#
# Declaring the policy here removes both, and makes the result identical on
# Windows, Linux and macOS regardless of core.autocrlf and core.eol.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact regardless of the auto detection above: Qt translation catalogues
# and images must never be rewritten.
*.qm binary
*.png binary
